@@ -52,6 +58,43 @@
 
 SCRIPT UPDATES
 
+v4.11
+Requirements:
+- eggdrop 1.6.0 or later. On older versions the script now logs a message and doesn't load (instead of calling 'die'). Compatibility code for eggdrop 1.3/1.4 has been removed.
+
+Security fixes (core):
+- netjump: the server argument was passed through eval, so '.netjump -all host:port:[cmd]' (or a crafted netjump from a control bot) executed arbitrary Tcl on every netbot, even with nb_nettcl disabled.
+- netchanset: channel names and settings were passed through eval (channel names may contain '[' ']'), and need-* settings (which are Tcl scripts) were only blocked in the first position. Both fixed for local and remote use; -reload parses config lines as lists and skips need-*.
+- Reply commands (rnetinfo, rnettcl, rnetshell, rnetserv, rnetpass, rmservers, rmsreset) bypass the control-bot check by design but used the remote-supplied idx directly, letting any netbot write arbitrary text into any idx - including bot links (raw botnet protocol). Replies now only go to partyline CHAT idxs of +n users.
+- netupdate: any netbot could request arbitrary files (e.g. bot configs, the userfile) from the hub with an unsolicited 'send'; the hub now only serves updates it initiated, refuses paths containing '..', and the old unused 'rnetupdate initiate' handler was removed. The receiver now only accepts start/write/close/end from the bot it asked and only for file names it requested.
+- netpass: password tables only ever change bot records; remote single-user changes check the user exists. nb_randpass uses /dev/urandom when available and generates 12-16 character passwords.
+- Botnet framing: invalid sids caused Tcl errors; multipart buffers were shared between bots (keyed only by a random 1-999 sid) and never expired. Buffers are now per bot, size limited (nb_maxbuffer), cleared when a bot unlinks and expired after 5 minutes. Empty nb_key now disables the protocol instead of sending plaintext.
+- nb_cmdcast never broadcasts the arguments of .chpass, .newpass, .netpass, .pass, .tcl, .nettcl, .set or .chaddr.
+
+Bug fixes (core):
+- nb_control was a single global reset by every partyline login, so one owner logging in silently changed another owner's .netcontrol selection. Selections are now per partyline session.
+- Component load errors stopped all remaining components (and the rest of netbots.tcl's load) from loading; the remaining components now still load.
+- Switching nb_flag to 'b'/'all' with a rehash left .chattr unbound until restart.
+- The nb_update time bind used the year field as a day-of-week, so the update check never ran. It now runs daily and checks at most once a week, with a 10 second HTTP timeout and proper cleanup.
+- '.netchanset -reload' leaked a file handle if any config line errored, and ignored .netcontrol on the local bot.
+- netpass table generation errored when there were no other netbots; .components errored when no scripts were found.
+- netupdate temp files collided for files with the same name in different directories, write errors left transfers stuck, and empty files could never be sent.
+- nb_randport could loop forever on an invalid port range and built huge lists for large ranges.
+- .netjump <bot> now works for the local bot and checks the bot is linked.
+- Removed unused helper procs slindex and stl, and global temporaries (nb_tclarg etc.) used by nettcl.
+
+Component fixes:
+- sentinel.tcl: the *banqueue procs wiped the whole ban queue instead of removing one entry (missing '$'); killban/killchanban/killignore were passed whole ban/ignore records instead of masks; per-channel state is created on demand and removed for deleted channels; timers no longer error on removed channels; rlock messages from other bots are validated and rate limited (they could be used to flood notes); turning sl_bxsimul off with a rehash now stops the away timer; uname/id are no longer exec'd on every rehash; invalid sl_locktimes entries are ignored.
+- repeat.tcl: reset timers were scheduled before the settings were split ('utimer "" ...'); toggling rp_efficient with a rehash left timers calling procs with the wrong arguments; disabled checks still counted forever (memory growth); notice text kept the leading ':'.
+- botnetop.tcl: a 'thekey' message from any linked bot could make the bot JOIN (now requires a configured channel, an authorised bot and a pending key request); missing channel validation caused errors; bop_who entries are case-insensitive and capped; the bot no longer wipes all need-* channel settings on every load; arrays for removed channels are cleaned up; limit parsing handles '+lk' modes; strict-host may be absent (eggdrop 1.8+); removed dead code (bop_doTheOp, pre-1.6 branches).
+- chanlimit.tcl: limit parsing handles keyed channels ('+lk 50 key'); .startlimit with cl_timer 0; commands are logged.
+- mass.tcl: .mass kick ignored the default reason; an empty KICK was sent when nobody matched; .netmass now honours nb_owner.
+- mainserver.tcl: jump used an empty port when a main server had no port; the retry message printed '1' instead of channel names; replies use the safe reply path; net commands honour nb_owner.
+- extras.tcl: disabling ex_newuser with a rehash left .+bot/.+user/.adduser unbound; ex_cleanup uses glob instead of exec ls; .clearbans shows usage for bad arguments; .inviteall/.opall validate the nick.
+- logfile.tcl: .sendlog/.maillog could send any file (e.g. the userfile); they are now limited to log files. The e-mail address was passed to exec unvalidated, so an address such as '>file' redirected output (file overwrite); addresses are validated and the log is fed through a channel. Old time binds are removed on rehash.
+- aidle.tcl: toggling ai_uidle with a rehash left two message loops running; no message is sent to channels the bot isn't on or when there are no channels/messages.
+- superbitch.tcl: duplicated punishment code merged; deops are only queued when the bot is opped.
